  "basis": "Five maintenance warnings do not establish exploits. Test/WASI-only chains and absent API preconditions have exact caller evidence. Network/library findings remain affected upstream versions, but the normal local solver receives no network/file/process permission grants, remote/npm modules or provider secrets, and its packaged environment strips broker/logging/telemetry overrides. RSA timing lacks a persistent provider private-key/decryption service. Fresh ordinary API probes observe no loopback traffic and denied environment access. No known finding remains without a scoped disposition. Future V8/native issues and same-user malware remain residual risks, not a mathematical-safety claim. Actual confirmed newly reachable issues require remediation.",
